ntrol is unusual for labs and shows imaginative reuse of existing DevOps tooling. Score 3\n\nacceptability_evidence: Automating regulatory documentation with internal data pipelines violates no legal, social or business norms and is a commonly accepted compliance practice. Score 4\n\nimplementability_evidence: Building CI/CD extractors for hyperparameters, dataset metadata and validation results requires moderate engineering changes but uses standard tooling labs already operate. Score 3\n\napplicability_evidence: The proposal directly targets the EU AI Act requirement to keep up-to-date technical documentation by converting R&D artifacts into compliant reports. Score 4\n\neffectiveness_evidence: Real-time synthesis will reduce manual record-keeping and improve documentation traceability, but it does not by itself guarantee the Article 12 event-logging capabilities for high-risk system use. Score 3\n\nReturn JSON? Instruction says return rating echoing its id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>. Probably output list.\n\nProvide formatted.\n\n",
