d to stated problem? Stated problem is meet logging mandate. Technical documentation is related but Article 12 is logs. Recital 71 links both. The proposal mentions transforms raw experiment logs. Might be 4? Could be 3 = solves implied problem related. Hmm.\n\nThe mandate is automatic recording of events logs over lifetime, and logging capabilities enable recording events relevant for identifying risk, post-market monitoring, monitoring operation. Proposal is about technical documentation engine capturing hyperparameters etc and compiling compliance reports. That's more about Recital 71 technical documentation, not Article 12 logging events.\n\nBut it does say transforms raw experiment logs into structured format suitable for regulators. Might be partially applicable.\n\nProbably applicability = 3? Or 4? \"solves an identified problem that is directly related to the stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of the stated problem)\". Y is meeting logging mandate. Does automated technical documentation engine meet logging mandate? It captures hyperparameters... Not necessarily logs events per Article 12(2)(a)(b)(c) and 3(a)-(d). So maybe only partially.\n\nI think applicability = 3: solves implied problem related to stated problem (do X to get implied Y, which applies to stated problem). The implied Y is keeping technical documentation up to date, which is part of traceability requirement in Recital 71 linked to record-keeping.\n\nLet's choose 3.\n\nEvidence sentence: The proposal targets real-time capture of development metadata and automated compliance reports, which addresses the documentation aspect of traceability referenced in Recital 71 linked to Article 12's record-keeping mandate.\n\nEffectiveness (1-4): degree to which idea will solve problem. 4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability. 3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution partial.\n\nWill automated technical documentation engine solve logging mandate? It helps 