ON? Instruction says return rating echoing its id exactly. For each subscale... give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first and then \"<subscale>\"...\n\nWe can output lines.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid: P1601\noriginality_evidence: ...\noriginality: 2\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\neffectiveness_evidence: ...\neffectiveness: 4\napplicability_evidence: ...\napplicability: 4\nimplementability_evidence: ...\nimplementability: 3\nacceptability_evidence: ...\nacceptability: 4\n\nMake sure one sentence evidence each.\n\nProvide concise.\n\nLet's craft sentences.\n\noriginality evidence: The tool automates versioned reference database logging for Annex III matches, a specific logging utility that is interesting but aligns with common compliance engineering practices.\n\nparadigm_relatedness evidence: It adds a new indexing utility but still treats compliance as a separate logging practice rather than weaving it into R&D or changing the lab’s research relationship.\n\neffectiveness evidence: By timestamping queries against versioned snapshots it creates an immutable link that directly meets Article 12(3)(b)-(c) traceability requirements for high-risk systems.\n\napplicability evidence: The proposal directly addresses how to meet the Article 12 logging mandate for Annex III high-risk AI systems in the lab’s R&D context.\n\nimplementability evidence: Building a versioned snapshot indexing service with immutable query timestamps requires non-trivial engineering changes but is reasonably feasible for an R&D lab.\n\nacceptability evidence: Automated compliance logging that satisfies EU legal requirements violates no norms and reflects common acceptable business practice.\n\nReturn.\n\n",
