ligations, OR addresses larger problem of what lab researches. The proposal changes relationship: traceability treated as primary objective of system quality. That is change relationship. Does it introduce new elements? Yes, audit step. Might be paradigm stretching vs breaking. Breaking says introduces new elements AND changes relationship... That's essentially same as stretching? Hmm distinction: stretching changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science). Breaking introduces new elements AND changes relationship, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches. Maybe breaking is stronger: changes what lab researches. This proposal doesn't change what they research, just how they validate. So likely 3 = paradigm stretching.\n\noriginality (1-4):\n4 = not expressed before AND ingenious...\n3 = unusual, interesting; shows some imagination\n2 = interesting\n1 = common, mundane\n\nIntegrated compliance validation pipeline is fairly standard DevOps practice applied to AI Act. Might be unusual but not ingenious? Could be 2 = interesting. Or 3 = unusual, interesting; shows some imagination. I'd say it's interesting but not surprising; CI checks for logs is common. So maybe 2.\n\nLet's pick 2.\n\napplicability (1-4):\n4 = solves identified problem directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem)\n3 = solves implied problem...\nProposal: how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Proposal does implement mandatory traceability audit step to verify logs generated correctly, simulate high-risk events. Directly addresses logging mandate. So 4.\n\neffectiveness (1-4):\n4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability\n3 = reasonable and will contribute...\nWill it solve? It ensures logs generated correctly. It doesn't guarantee logs meet Article 12 specifics like period of each use etc., but seems reasonable. Might be partial solution? Probably will contribute to solution, not fully solve