e 12(3) linking input matches... That's fairly common compliance tool. Probably common, mundane. Maybe interesting? Could be 2? The proposal is essentially building a logging DB interface for biometric systems. That's expected. Might be common. I'd say originality = 1 or 2. \"common, mundane, boring\" fits. It is standard audit module. Likely 1.\n\neffectiveness (1-4): degree to which idea will solve problem.\n4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability\n3 = reasonable and will contribute...\n2 = unreasonable or unlikely...\n1 = solves unrelated problem\n\nIt directly satisfies most stringent legal requirements. It addresses logging mandate for Annex III. That would solve problem of meeting logging mandate for those systems. Reasonable and will solve. Probably 4.\n\napplicability (1-4): degree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem.\n4 = solves an identified problem that is directly related to stated problem\n3 = solves implied problem...\nIt directly satisfies legal requirements to maintain market reputation. That's directly related. Score 4.\n\nacceptability (1-4): degree to which idea is socially, legally, politically acceptable.\n4 = common strategies that violate no norms\n3 = somewhat uncommon...\nProposal is building secure database interface linking input matches to human verifiers. Acceptable? Possibly privacy concerns? Linking identification... But within legal mandate. Probably common strategies. Score 4.\n\nimplementability (1-4): degree to which idea can be easily implemented.\n4 = easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes\n3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\n2 = significant change, or expensive/difficult...\nBuilding specialized data capture tool tailored specifically... mandatory for all Annex III projects. That's significant change? Might be some changes, reasonably feasible. Could be 3. Not easy low cost. Secure database interface linking matches... That's moderate. I'd say 3 = some