blem of what lab researches\n3 paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners...)\n2 slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way unchanged\n\nThis is a targeted research project to minimize overhead. It's introducing new elements tools? It's still treats compliance as logging practice, just optimize. Probably slightly paradigm stretching? Or paradigm preserving? It introduces benchmarking study, maybe new process. Might be 2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. Could be 1 = standard compliance practice. Hmm optimization study is fairly standard. I think 2.\n\nOriginality: degree to which idea is rare but ingenious... 4 not expressed before AND ingenious... 3 unusual interesting shows some imagination 2 interesting 1 common mundane boring\n\nLog optimization performance study is common, mundane. Probably 1 = common, mundane, boring.\n\nAcceptability: degree socially legally politically acceptable. Common strategies that violate no norms. 4 = common strategies that violate no norms or sensibilities. Yes. So 4.\n\nImplementability: degree can be easily implemented. Easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes? A targeted research project to benchmark logging granularities and compression. That's some changes, reasonably feasible measures. Could be 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures. Might be 3 not 4 because requires research time. Probably 3.\n\nWe need format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>. Possibly JSON? Instruction says return rating... For each subscale... give \"..._evidence\" first and then \"...\". Likely output lines.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid: P1110\napplicability_evidence: ...\napplicability: