n into science, new partners...). 2 slightly paradigm stretching introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. 1 paradigm preserving standard compliance.\n\nAutomated documentation sync pipeline introduces tool but still treats compliance as documentation practice. Probably slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice? Actually documentation not logging. Might be 2. Could be 2 = introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. Yes.\n\nOriginality: degree rare but ingenious. Not expressed before AND ingenious =4. Unusual interesting shows some imagination =3. Interesting=2. Common mundane=1. Automated pipeline converting experiment tracking to compliance docs is fairly common idea. Might be common. Probably 2 = interesting? Or 1 = common mundane boring. Many labs talk about auto doc generation. I'd say 2 interesting, or 1 common. Let's pick 2? Hmm.\n\nThe reference class is responses experienced evaluator would expect AI R&D labs to give to this mandate. Automated documentation sync is fairly expected. Might be common mundane. Could be 1 = common mundane boring. I'd lean 2 = interesting.\n\nLet's choose originality 2.\n\nProvide output format: echo id, then for each subscale evidence sentence then score.\n\nProbably JSON? Instruction says return rating echoing its id exactly. For each subscale give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first and then \"<subscale>\". Could be plain text lines.\n\nWe'll produce:\n\nid: P2274\nimplementability_evidence: ...\nimplementability: 3\n...\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nLet's craft sentences concise.\n\nImplementability evidence: Integration of existing MLflow and version control with a reporting tool for auto-generated dossiers is technically feasible with standard engineering effort. Score 3.\n\nAcceptability evidence: Automating compliance paperwork aligns with regulatory