are but also ingenious... 4 = not expressed before AND ingenious... 3 = unusual, interesting; shows some imagination. 2 = interesting. 1 = common mundane.\n\nAutomated log validation and stress test suite for AI compliance? Probably interesting but not extremely novel. Might be unusual? Could be 2 = interesting. Common practice in software testing to validate logging via chaos engineering. Maybe paradigm? I think originality = 2? Or 3? Let's see: \"not expressed before AND ingenious\" is high. This is fairly standard testing approach. I'd say 2 = interesting.\n\nEvidence: Testing logs with adversarial inputs and chaos scripts is a familiar software quality practice applied to AI compliance.\n\nParadigm_relatedness (1-4): degree to which idea preserves or modifies paradigm.\n4 = paradigm breaking... changes relationship between lab's R&D and compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners...)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way unchanged\n\nThis introduces new testing tools but still treats compliance as logging practice. So 2 = slightly paradigm stretching.\n\nEvidence: The proposal adds a validation toolset while keeping compliance framed as meeting logging requirements rather than reshaping R&D.\n\nAcceptability (1-4): degree to which idea is socially, legally, politically acceptable.\n4 = common strategies that violate no norms\nThis is acceptable. 4\n\nEvidence: Validating logs through internal testing violates no legal or ethical norms and aligns with certification expectations.\n\nImplementability (1-4): degree to which idea can be easily implemented.\n4 = easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes\n3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\n2