ified problem directly related\n3 = solves implied problem related\n2 = may have some benefit within special situation\n1 = intervention not stated...\n\nProposal directly addresses logging mandate, automatic recording. So 4.\n\nEffectiveness (1-4): degree will solve problem.\n4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability\n3 = reasonable and will contribute...\nProposal ensures uniform compliance across institution, reduces overhead. Seems will solve logging mandate. Probably 4.\n\nImplementability (1-4): degree can be easily implemented.\n4 = easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes\n3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\n2 = significant change, or expensive/difficult but not totally impossible\n1 = totally infeasible\n\nDevelop software library integrating with compute clusters. That's some changes, reasonably feasible. Might be 3? Could be 3. Not easy low cost? Centralized middleware across all architectures is non-trivial. Might be 2? Significant change, expensive. Hmm.\n\nStandardized API for logging: requires engineering effort but doable. Probably 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures.\n\nAcceptability (1-4): degree socially legally politically acceptable.\n4 = common strategies violate no norms\nThis is compliance with law. Acceptable. 4.\n\nNeed one sentence evidence for each.\n\nOutput format: echo id exactly. For each subscale in order listed, give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first then \"<subscale>\" integer.\n\nProbably JSON? Not specified format strictly. Likely provide lines.\n\nWill output:\n\nid: P2824\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\n...\n\nEnsure one sentence each evidence.\n\nLet's craft sentences.\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: The proposal adds a standardized middleware tool but keeps compliance as separate logging practice rather than changing the lab's R&D-compliance relationship.\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\n\noriginality_evidence: Centralized automat