s somewhat common in regulated industries (gate funding). Might be common. Probably 2 = interesting, or 1 = common mundane. Might be somewhat uncommon but not surprising. I'd say 2? Or 3? Could be unusual. Let's say 2 = interesting.\n\nBetter to pick 2 for originality: it's a known management technique applied to AI compliance.\n\nThus scores:\nacceptability 4\nimplementability 3 (maybe 4?). Let's decide implementability 3 = some changes or reasonably feasible measures. Updating quarterly review criteria is easy? Might be easy to implement at low cost, non-radical changes =4. Hmm. Updating budget allocation process might be moderate. I'd lean 3.\n\nLet's output format: echo id. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nProbably need lines.\n\nReturn rating.\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence for each.\n\nProvide final JSON? Probably just list.\n\nI'll produce:\n\nid P1488\nacceptability_evidence: ...\nacceptability: 4\n...\n\nLet's do.\n\n",
