elf. It contributes to ensuring compliance, but does not directly implement logs. Might be partial solution. So 3 = reasonable and will contribute.\n\nEvidence: Verifying log capture improves confidence in compliance but does not by itself create the required logging capability.\n\nScore 3.\n\napplicability (1-4): degree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem.\n4 = solves an identified problem that is directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem)\nIdea directly relates to Article 12 logging mandate. Simulates real-world deployment to verify logs correctly capture risk events as required. That's directly related. So 4.\n\nEvidence: The suite directly targets Article 12's requirement for logs to record risk events and enable traceability.\n\nScore 4.\n\nReturn rating echoing id exactly. Provide subscale_evidence then subscale.\n\nFormat? Probably lines.\n\nNeed for each subscale: first write one sentence of evidence... THEN give its score as integer level.\n\nOutput JSON? Probably just list.\n\nI'll output:\n\nid: P1920\noriginality_evidence: ...\noriginality: 3 etc.\n\nEnsure order.\n\nLet's produce.",
